# Keep corrections as rules

When the user states a constraint that later sessions must follow, do not stop at the local edit. Add or update an `.mdc` file under `.cursor/rules/`.

A correction given in the conversation lands in the same change. A lesson first noticed at the post-merge retrospective becomes a rule without waiting for an ask: a `chore` Issue and a rules PR right after the retrospective (`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`). Tacit knowledge the work relied on, which no rule states yet, counts as such a lesson.

## Record

- A way of writing, a procedure, or a prohibition that would be corrected again next time
- Anything the user marks as ongoing, including 「今後も」 and "make this a rule"

## Do not record here

- A one-off fix in a single file
- The design specification. Write that in `docs/design.ja.md` and `docs/design.md` together. A rule only says to follow the spec
- A transcript of an external review

## Shape

- One concern per file. Keep it short. Include a before and after example
- `alwaysApply: true` when every session needs it
- `globs` and `alwaysApply: false` when it applies to specific files

Figures and formulas in the design spec belong in `dev-docs.mdc` (`docs/design.md`, `docs/design.ja.md`). This file stays `alwaysApply: true`.

```text
# BAD — fix the sentence and move on
User: この手の後回しは、次からも時期を書きなさい
Agent: edits the one paragraph

# GOOD — the ongoing constraint becomes a rule in the same change
User: この手の後回しは、次からも時期を書きなさい
Agent: edits the paragraph and updates .cursor/rules/defer.mdc
```
